{"id": "EUVD-2026-86027", "enisaUuid": "c8fb71ae-5d4f-3617-b81e-63c3d63f8590", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: mediatek: mt8365-afe-pcm: fix possible NULL-pointer dereferences in mt8365_afe_suspend()\n\nmt8365_afe_suspend() allocates the register backup buffer with\ndevm_kcalloc(), but does not check for allocation failure before using the\nreturned pointer. This may lead to a NULL pointer dereference when\naccessing afe->reg_back_up[i].\n\nAdd the missing NULL check and return -ENOMEM on allocation failure after\ndisabling the main clock.\n\nAlso propagate the return value of mt8365_afe_suspend() in\nmt8365_afe_dev_runtime_suspend() so that the suspended state is not updated\nwhen suspend fails.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T12:43:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f87707bc0406fe92bc142a9eee5f480c94ce9ff8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1094d83ad325829acd68e63147793536060a0d60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8948ac26efc395264a47f9a743889065adb5cff"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cfm8-jq8w-4xxp", "CVE-2026-97414"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "116d273c-9bda-3ae0-b52f-c71a9e383f46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1fa7ec52-10e0-3dda-b1aa-6fd31b126a44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "562fef41-bb7b-3d58-bdbf-366d4a532172", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1991d102bc2abb32331c462f8f3e77059c69578 <1094d83ad325829acd68e63147793536060a0d60"}, {"id": "72823527-b9b9-3835-90b5-5ce4a610f9ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1991d102bc2abb32331c462f8f3e77059c69578 <b8948ac26efc395264a47f9a743889065adb5cff"}, {"id": "944da21e-0fa6-36f7-bbd1-2fa4e614cb91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "98307e2a-aebe-3688-9d11-6dca496328d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "ab9ea160-aeba-3116-a1cf-fb62e504425f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "f670de96-1e5a-3533-9551-3464d01cf2b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1991d102bc2abb32331c462f8f3e77059c69578 <f87707bc0406fe92bc142a9eee5f480c94ce9ff8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3a6307c8-f715-3444-a342-17cd6d198fef", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}